<title>PARAGUAY: Paraguay Congress approves bond issues.</title>
<headline>Paraguay Congress approves bond issues.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay's Congress on Thursday approved a government plan to issue $150 million in bonds through the end of 1997.</p>
<p>No date has been set for the issues, but $50 million will be issued this year and $100 million next year.</p>
<p>The bonds, to be issued in Paraguay, may be denominated in either dollars or the local currency, the Guarani.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to finance social projects.</p>
<p>-- Jose Maria Amarilla, Asuncion Newsroom, (59521) 444527</p>
